# Paths Semgrep does not scan. Owner: Security agent.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A LINE
# Every entry here removes a path from EVERY rule at once, including rules written years
# from now by people who will never read this file. That makes it the bluntest instrument
# in the security toolchain, so it is reserved for code this repository does not author:
# vendored dependencies, build output, and binary assets.
#
# It is NOT the place for:
#   * a false positive          -> fix the rule, or suppress the line with `# nosemgrep: <rule-id> - <reason>`
#   * a rule that is too noisy  -> scope it with `paths.exclude` inside the rule itself
#   * test files                -> tests get scanned. A vulnerability in a test fixture is
#                                  still a vulnerability, and test code is where hardcoded
#                                  credentials go to be forgotten. Where a rule genuinely
#                                  cannot apply to tests (the masking-salt KAT vectors),
#                                  the carve-out lives in .semgrep/contracts.yml, scoped to
#                                  that one rule.

